    "title": "Prichard water board reports overflows, issues water advisory - NewsBreak",
    "text": "PRICHARD, Ala. ( WKRG ) — Heavy rains Tuesday caused multiple wastewater overflows in Prichard, resulting in a water advisory. According to a Prichard Water Works and Sewer Board news release, the following areas are affected with the following estimated overflows: Mobile County Health Officer Dr. Kevin Michaels advises area residents to take precautions if they come into contact with any standing water that may have accumulated because of the overflows, and make sure they wash their hands and clothing thoroughly. Additionally, residents should avoid using Chickasaw Creek, Gum Tree Branch and Toulmins Spring Branch for recreational activities because of the overflows, the release said. Any seafood harvested in those areas should be cooked thoroughly before being eaten, according to the release. People should wash their hands anytime they’ve cleaned seafood before preparing food. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
